<!doctype html>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>ReconPilot — verification</title>
<link rel="icon" href="data:,">
<style>
:root{--ink:#12181f;--muted:#5a6673;--line:#dfe4ea;--bg:#f7f8fa;--ok:#0a6b3d;--okbg:#e6f4ec;--bad:#8a1c1c;--badbg:#fbeaea}
*{box-sizing:border-box}
body{margin:0;padding:32px 20px 64px;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);
font:16px/1.55 system-ui,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif}
main{max-width:860px;margin:0 auto}
h1{font-size:22px;margin:0 0 4px}
.sub{color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 28px}
.verdict{border-radius:10px;padding:18px 20px;margin:0 0 28px;border:1px solid}
.verdict.ok{background:var(--okbg);border-color:#bcdccb;color:var(--ok)}
.verdict.bad{background:var(--badbg);border-color:#e5bcbc;color:var(--bad)}
.verdict b{font-size:19px;display:block;margin-bottom:4px}
.claims{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(230px,1fr));gap:12px;margin:0 0 30px}
.claim{background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;padding:14px 16px}
.claim .n{font-size:24px;font-weight:650;letter-spacing:-.01em}
.claim .n.ok{color:var(--ok)}
.claim .n.bad{color:var(--bad)}
.claim .t{color:var(--muted);font-size:14px;margin-top:2px}
h2{font-size:15px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;color:var(--muted);
margin:32px 0 10px;font-weight:650}
table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line);
border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden}
th,td{padding:10px 14px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);font-size:15px}
th{background:#fbfcfd;font-weight:600;color:var(--muted);font-size:13px;
text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em}
tr:last-child td{border-bottom:0}
td.num,th.num{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
td.note{color:var(--muted);font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.45}
.flag{display:inline-block;font-size:12px;font-weight:650;padding:1px 7px;border-radius:20px}
.flag.ok{background:var(--okbg);color:var(--ok)}
.flag.bad{background:var(--badbg);color:var(--bad)}
dl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;gap:6px 18px;margin:0;background:#fff;
border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;padding:16px 18px}
dt{color:var(--muted);font-size:14px}
dd{margin:0;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
.boundary{margin-top:32px;border-left:3px solid var(--line);padding:2px 0 2px 16px;
color:var(--muted);font-size:14.5px}
.boundary b{color:var(--ink)}
code{font:13.5px ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;background:#eef1f4;
padding:1px 5px;border-radius:4px}
</style>
<main>
<h1>ReconPilot — verification run</h1>
<p class="sub">Reconciliation over a seeded synthetic book, scored against the generator's ground
truth. Every figure below is measured by this run, not read from a file.</p>

{{if .Passed}}
<div class="verdict ok">
  <b>PASS</b>
  All injected discrepancy types were detected, no false match was produced, and every intended
  pair and group was matched in full.
</div>
{{else}}
<div class="verdict bad">
  <b>FAIL</b>
  At least one claim did not hold on this run. The rows marked below are the ones that fell short.
</div>
{{end}}

<div class="claims">
  <div class="claim">
    <div class="n {{if .TypesOK}}ok{{else}}bad{{end}}">{{.DetectedTypes}}/{{.InjectedTypes}}</div>
    <div class="t">injected discrepancy types detected</div>
  </div>
  <div class="claim">
    <div class="n {{if eq .FalseMatches 0}}ok{{else}}bad{{end}}">{{.FalseMatches}}</div>
    <div class="t">false matches</div>
  </div>
  <div class="claim">
    <div class="n {{if eq .MissedIntended 0}}ok{{else}}bad{{end}}">{{.MissedIntended}}</div>
    <div class="t">intended pairs or groups not fully matched</div>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>Detection by discrepancy type</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Type</th><th class="num">Injected</th><th class="num">Detected</th><th>Status</th></tr>
  {{range .Rows}}
  <tr>
    <td>{{.Type}}</td>
    <td class="num">{{.Injected}}</td>
    <td class="num">{{.Detected}}</td>
    <td>
      {{if .Short}}<span class="flag bad">under-detected</span>
      {{else}}<span class="flag ok">ok</span>{{end}}
    </td>
  </tr>
  {{if .Inflation}}
  <tr><td class="note" colspan="4">Detected exceeds injected by design: {{.Inflation}}.</td></tr>
  {{end}}
  {{end}}
</table>
<p class="boundary">Only under-detection counts as a failure. Where detection exceeds injection the
reason is stated on the row — those extra records are correct output, not noise.</p>

<h2>Match integrity</h2>
<dl>
  <dt>Clean pairs in the book</dt><dd>{{.CleanPairs}}</dd>
  <dt>Clean marketplace groups</dt><dd>{{.CleanGroups}}</dd>
  <dt>Matches produced</dt><dd>{{.Matches}}</dd>
  <dt>False matches</dt><dd>{{.FalseMatches}}</dd>
  <dt>Intended pairs or groups not fully matched</dt><dd>{{.MissedIntended}}</dd>
</dl>

<h2>Run parameters</h2>
<dl>
  <dt>Transactions</dt><dd>{{.N}}</dd>
  <dt>Generator seed</dt><dd>{{.Seed}}</dd>
  <dt>Engine time</dt><dd>{{.Elapsed}}</dd>
  <dt>Runtime invariants</dt><dd>passed — the engine returns no output when one is violated</dd>
</dl>

<p class="boundary"><b>What this proves, and what it does not.</b>
The book is synthetic and generated in-process by <code>internal/generator</code>, which also
supplies the ground truth used to score the result. That makes the claim reproducible by anyone —
the same seed produces the same book and the same numbers — and it means the figures measure the
engine's behaviour, not production mileage on real bank data. Re-run with a different
<code>-seed</code> to confirm the result is not seed-specific.</p>
</main>
